---
 

 <<PlayBackgroundMusic "Emotional_1">>
<<SetBGSprite hutInterior>>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Maa… Baba… can I talk for two minutes straight?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Two minutes from you becomes twenty, but sit beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: If it's about the rice, keep for morning. My head is heavy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: It's about Raju. I think we have a gem in the house.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Every mother thinks so.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: I'm not saying it like a brother, but as someone who watches the ground breathe - he sees the ball early, listens, shares, and doesn't shrink under pressure.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Nerves don't feed stomachs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: True, but I'm asking for time and routine - morning practice near the handpump, school on time, chores done, then study. If his marks fall, I'll lock this bat myself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Worried">>
Kamla: People will talk. "Poor folks and big dreams."

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Confident">>
Ramu: People laugh before they clap, Maa - let them finish both. We'll borrow discipline, not money, and it's free.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: What will it cost?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: One steel bottle of water, chalk for the crease, and my sleep - I'll take an extra hour at the tire repair shop to buy second-hand pads later.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: And studies? His teacher already said his handwriting runs like a train.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Then we slow the train - half hour every night with poem, dictation, and tables. If he misses, he misses the ground next day.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Hope is a dangerous thing, Ramu.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: False hope is, but this is measured - three months of routine and if he lights up the lane, we talk to Masterji about district trials.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Worried">>
Kamla: He is small.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Determined">>
Ramu: Small hands learn courage faster - he already keeps the bat face up when it rests and breathed through the pressure like I taught. Eight-year-olds don't fake that.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Curious">>
ShivPrasad: You speak like a coach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Serious">>
Ramu: Because our lane doesn't have one, so I'll be it while keeping my marks decent - Friday nights, both of us read to you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Worried">>
Kamla: What if he gets hurt?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Then we learn why and fix it - we don't let poverty steal our manners or our safety.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: And what do you want from me?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Permission, and when neighbors scoff, say "He's practicing habits, not chasing cricket."

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Curious">>
Kamla: Tell me one more time—what do you see in him?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Proud">>
Ramu: I see a boy who hears the ground, waits when waiting is heavy, and smiles after a miss - that comes from inside, not posters.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Curious">>
ShivPrasad: Dreams make the room feel bigger, huh?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Only if we open the window a little - dawn to the handpump, I'll chalk the line and he'll carry the water.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: I say three months - no money wasted, marks and manners steady, or game over.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Deal. I'll keep score on both.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Proud">>
ShivPrasad: And tell the boy—when he steps out, he carries us with him. Not our burden—our blessing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Loving">>
Kamla: Go sleep. Morning comes fast to those with promises.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Relieved">>
Ramu: Promises wake me faster. Good night, Maa. Good night, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Loving">>
Kamla: Good night, coach. Good Night Hope.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
<<StopBackgroundMusic>>
